 The entry script uses `@tool`, so it runs inside the editor. Full design and CLI
 docs: <https://github.com/NotNull92/hera-agent-godot>.
+
+## External runtime targeting
+
+Game requests may include a positive integral `pid` in their params. A fresh
+matching runtime heartbeat is required; without `pid`, the existing editor-play
+selection and ambiguity checks are unchanged. CLI integration is one field:
+`hera game --pid <PID> ...` must send `{"tool":"game","params":{"pid":PID,...}}`.
+
+For portrait runtimes taller than macOS permits for a titled window, launch the
+bounded borderless runner with the installed Godot binary:
+
+```bash
+Godot --display-driver macos --audio-driver Dummy --rendering-method gl_compatibility \
+  --path /path/to/project --resolution 1080x1920 --fixed-fps 60 --disable-vsync \
+  --script res://addons/hera_agent_godot/runtime/external_launcher.gd -- \
+  res://game/Main.tscn 1080 1920 1900 20
+```
+
+The five runner arguments are scene, width, height, x, and y. The scene must be
+a `res://` `.tscn`; dimensions are limited to 64–4096 and positions to ±8192.
